WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.560
When it comes to modern-day action stars,&nbsp;
a few names always have to enter the mix.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.040
Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson follows in the long,&nbsp;
storied tradition of larger-than-life figures.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:13.120
Honestly, anyone who's been in a "Fast &amp;&nbsp;
Furious" movie falls into that category,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:17.200
and that goes double with one of the hardest&nbsp;
working men in Hollywood — Jason Statham.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.720
Throughout the 21st century, he's starred&nbsp;
in some of the most critically-acclaimed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:26.000
heist and action flicks, such as "The Italian&nbsp;
Job," "Crank," and "War." When you walk into a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.160
Statham movie, you know exactly what you're&nbsp;
getting, but not every film can be a hit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:33.920
Others fall off the radar, but older&nbsp;
movies have managed to find a second life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:38.080
thanks to the glut of streaming services as&nbsp;
of late. That's the case for the underrated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:41.440
Statham movie "Chaos," which&nbsp;
is now making waves on Netflix.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:46.320
The movie only grossed $7 million globally during&nbsp;
its run, but now's your chance of seeing what you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:51.120
missed 16 years ago. See why the film has&nbsp;
broken into the platform's Top 10 Movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.600
especially if you're a fan&nbsp;
of Statham's other works.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:58.160
Statham plays a veteran detective named Quentin&nbsp;
Conners who is reprimanded and then quickly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:02.800
reinstated onto the force when a group of&nbsp;
criminals takes hostages in a bank. He's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:07.120
teamed up with rookie cop Shane Dekker, and things&nbsp;
take a turn for the worse when they discover the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:11.920
thieves uploaded a computer virus into the&nbsp;
bank's systems capable of random evolution.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.920
The virus follows the principles of chaos&nbsp;
theory, which is where the film gets its name,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:19.920
so it's a race against the clock for the&nbsp;
officers to figure out a way to stop the attack.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:23.280
You'd be forgiven for missing the film&nbsp;
when it first came out. It didn't receive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:27.600
a theatrical release in the United States,&nbsp;
going straight-to-video instead. That's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:31.920
bit of a surprise, considering that Statham's&nbsp;
star was on the rise in the early 2000s thanks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:36.560
to his appearance in movies like "The Transporter"&nbsp;
series and "The Italian Job." And that's not even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:41.520
to mention the fact that Ryan Phillippe and Wesley&nbsp;
Snipes, themselves well-known actors at the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:46.240
co-star in the movie. The few critics that&nbsp;
did review "Chaos" were mostly underwhelmed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:50.800
but that only paints half a picture in regard to&nbsp;
how the film has been received over the years.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:54.240
Reel Film gave the movie two stars&nbsp;
out of five and complained that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:57.760
movie's occasional moments of strong&nbsp;
action filmmaking were otherwise,

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:02.320
"Bogged down with an overwrought and&nbsp;
overplayed sensibility that proves disastrous."

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:05.440
The outlet said the movie lacked&nbsp;
originality and concluded,

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:09.840
"The equally impressive performances&nbsp;
ensure that boredom never entirely sets in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:11.760
though it's awfully difficult to look past the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:15.840
almost laughably inept instances of&nbsp;
plotting within Giglio's screenplay."

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:20.640
The film did have its defenders, though. Fernby&nbsp;
Films enjoyed Statham's performance and noted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.800
"it's got some delightfully done set-pieces&nbsp;
..." They concluded their review by writing,

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:26.560
"While I wasn't expecting a whole lot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:30.400
what I got was thoroughly enjoyable and&nbsp;
most definitely a film worth watching."

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:34.480
So, all in all, a pretty mixed-to-negative&nbsp;
response from critics. When it comes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:38.480
audience reactions though, movie-goers&nbsp;
seemed to enjoy the Statham action flick.

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:42.560
With a movie like "Chaos," critical reception&nbsp;
should be taken with a grain of salt.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:46.480
After all, not everyone is tuning into a&nbsp;
Statham headliner for strong characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:50.320
and an intricate plot. And for&nbsp;
movie fans who left reviews on IMDB,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:54.160
the consensus seems to be that&nbsp;
"Chaos" is, all in all, a fun watch.

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:55.360
One user said,

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:59.040
"All the signs were pointing to this&nbsp;
being a bad movie. It is fun to watch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:03.760
and the film does present [an] intriguing mystery&nbsp;
with a few surprising twists along the way."

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:07.360
Another user also had a fun time&nbsp;
with "Chaos" despite their nitpicks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:11.040
They loved the movie's "twists and turns"&nbsp;
and while they did take issue with some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.440
of the character choices, they ultimately said,

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:14.800
"But for a popcorn thriller,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:19.120
this was quite entertaining. Any film with&nbsp;
Statham in it is always worth a watch."

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:22.320
With the movie currently killing it&nbsp;
on Netflix, it looks like audiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:26.080
are in agreement that "Chaos" is one&nbsp;
forgotten gem that's worth checking out.

